P axial |det| = 12/r**4  (P 3.2 says 12/r^4)
chain axial |det| = r**(-4)  (046 (4): r^-3 * r^-1 for t-gradient pair = r^-4)
transverse pair |det| both: (1/2,1/2;-1/r,1/r) -> 1/r
V-corr + U3/12 = 0
P target: [b - k*r**3/2, -k*r**2, 0, 12*k]  (P 3.3: b-kr^3/2, -kr^2, 0, 12k)
chain target: [b - kappa*r**3/12, -kappa/6, 0, 0]  (046 (5): b-kappa r^3/12, -kappa/6, 0, 0)
U3 ->  c3  ; V-corr -> -c3/12  (c3 = f_ttt)
P/chain full Jacobian ratio: 12 => 12*pi_U3 = p_u, consistent with |dU3/du|=12
